egin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =4-1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305055 13194139534714 true] [17592186305054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305056 13194139534714 true] [17592186305054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305057 13194139534714 true] [17592186305054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305058 13194139534714 true] [17592186305054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305059 13194139534714 true] [17592186305054 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534714 true] [17592186305054 1041 "selection" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305054 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305058 13194139534714 true] [17592186305054 1110 #uuid "84690231-57c0-5dab-af90-fa45238c5de9" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305055 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305055 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305055 1111 #uuid "51366a49-fd12-5786-8f7d-f07bc638c401" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305056 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305056 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305056 1111 #uuid "997c191b-7355-5162-8345-97f79fb7d478" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305057 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305057 1111 #uuid "437df922-4149-5cc6-94d7-2f7829f9639e" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305058 1034 "I only" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305058 1111 #uuid "40f5ebcd-03b2-513b-839f-8c5b12075845" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305059 1034 "II only" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305059 1111 #uuid "5718d1cc-559e-5b30-ac50-6efe49b4568a" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305060 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305061 13194139534714 true] [17592186305060 1089 "q-158428" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305060 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534714 true] [17592186305060 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040017/assets/6e540dc9309f2a5d1753760b4050c049e380705914d7289b47319de0b0696a9a.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}4({x}^{3}-1),\\, & \\frac{1}{2}<x\\le \\frac{3}{2}, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n- ${\\int }_{1/2}^{3/2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305060 1113 #uuid "135e16d9-b89b-5e2d-b1ba-1746dcd48867" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305060 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. $f(x)$ is negative for some value of $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{3/2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{3/2}4({x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{1/2}^{3/2}({x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-x]}_{1/2}^{3/2} \\\\  & =4([\\frac{81}{64}-\\frac{3}{2}]-[\\frac{1}{64}-\\frac{1}{2}]) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{80}{64}-1) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{5}{4}-1) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement I is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305062 13194139534714 true] [17592186305061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305063 13194139534714 true] [17592186305061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305064 13194139534714 true] [1759218630506