f the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305067 1113 #uuid "6c7c7a03-37ed-5514-b67b-267ee6ad6e74" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305067 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, we see that $f(x)$ is nonnegative for all $x.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}-x]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[9-3]-[1-1] \\\\  & =6-0 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305069 13194139534714 true] [17592186305068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305070 13194139534714 true] [17592186305068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305071 13194139534714 true] [17592186305068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305072 13194139534714 true] [17592186305068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305073 13194139534714 true] [17592186305068 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534714 true] [17592186305068 1041 "selection" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305068 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305072 13194139534714 true] [17592186305068 1110 #uuid "93f7fbea-2b76-5d32-969a-94f326a9b2b7" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305069 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305069 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305069 1111 #uuid "abbf513f-2d0b-5290-8b2f-73bb25611fd0" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305070 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305070 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305070 1111 #uuid "308e70fd-a