186305108 1111 #uuid "464fb7ed-f856-5245-9633-4bbf6e183eb3" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305109 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305110 13194139534714 true] [17592186305109 1089 "q-87160" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305109 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534714 true] [17592186305109 1100 "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n\n- The volume of milk produced by a particular cow on a randomly selected day, measured in liters\n- The outcome of rolling a $6$-sided die\n- The distance that a randomly selected runner can run in $30$ minutes" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305109 1113 #uuid "0e3a4770-f26a-5c48-b3f0-e6bca8bc6054" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305109 1145 "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040017/assets/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real numbers in the interval $(0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $1,2,3,…,6,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement III describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real numbers in the interval $(0,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305111 13194139534714 true] [17592186305110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305112 13194139534714 true] [17592186305110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305113 13194139534714 true] [17592186305110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305114 13194139534714 true] [17592186305110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305115 13194139534714 true] [17592186305110 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534714 true] [17592186305110 1041 "selection" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305110 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305112 13194139534714 true] [17592186305110 1110 #uuid "a5fe2173-d9b4-5f3b-b6cd-ba715b63e8f8" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305111 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305111 1111 #uuid "2f96abd4-1370-585a-a52b-3f9601898726" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305112 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305112 1111 #uuid "1cf9c9af-a111-59cb-83ca-9fffd32ae6a0" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305113 1034 "I only" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305113 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305113 1111 #uuid "6d2377dc-878d-5277-996f-e7edfffaf2bf" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305114 1034 "III only" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305114 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305114 1111 #uuid "54c2c62d-369e-591b-873b-0fd358282f3f" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305115 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534714 true] [17592186305115 1111 #uuid "56cb22d8-667b-5a71-b823-aea3823d1f8b" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305116 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305117 13194139534714 true] [17592186305116 1089 "q-87236" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305116 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534714 true] [17592186305116 1100 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{{x}^{3}},\\, & 3<x<6, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305116 1113 #uuid "e88718f2-773a-5bee-bcb1-ba3ae7c0536e" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305116 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nFor the given function, the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{k}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{k}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}k{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{k}{2{x}^{2}}]}_{3}^{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k}{72}+\\frac{k}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{24}=1\\,⟹\\,k=24.\n$$" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305118 13194139534714 true] [17592186305117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305119 13194139534714 true] [17592186305117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305120 13194139534714 true] [17592186305117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305121 13194139534714 true] [17592186305117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305122 13194139534714 true] [17592186305117 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534714 true] [17592186305117 1041 "selection" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305117 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305122 13194139534714 true] [17592186305117 1110 #uuid "25fd1f61-d76e-5824-842e-ab1a3a1e9d5e" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305118 1034 "12" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305118 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534714 true] [17592186305118 1111 #uuid "455d74f5-6fac-51b6-b06e-3d78221c1199" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305119 1034 "\\frac{1}{24}" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534714 true] [17592186305119 1111 #uuid "7c168dc6-a35b-59b3-9c1b-fed3f4c924f5" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305120 1034 "8" 13194139534714 true] [17592186305120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534714 true] [17592186305120 1111 #uuid "f05e5822-5d83-57d9-a